So that the letter you send us is the letter we can close on, here is the s=
taff's position stated plainly.<br />
<br />
Rule 206(4)-2(d)(2)(ii) treats as custody any arrangement under which the a=
dviser is authorized to withdraw client funds or securities maintained with=
 a custodian upon the adviser's instruction to the custodian. Section 5(b) =
of your executed advisory agreement authorizes exactly that. The analysis d=
oes not depend on whether the firm could have taken more than its stated fe=
e, and the fee-debit accommodation the firm has been relying on did not sur=
vive the 2010 amendments.<br />
<br />
The consequence is the surprise examination requirement in paragraph (a)(4)=
, which the firm did not meet for 2010.<br />
<br />
On Mr. Halstead's question about scope, the staff will consider a defined-p=
eriod commitment. What the staff will not accept is a commitment that descr=
ibes remediation already completed and promises nothing about the conduct g=
oing forward.<br />
